    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the identity key as specified. Duplicate detection now runs off a single SHA-256 identity key, and the soft-match rule was widened accordingly.\n\n**New shared util \u2014 `util/IdentityKeys.java`:**\n- `identityKey(telephone, email, lastName)` = lower-case hex SHA-256 of `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (empty segment for absent telephone/email).\n- `soundex(name)` \u2014 a self-contained standard American Soundex implementation (no new dependency), with the h/w-collapse and vowel-separator rules.\n- `sha256Hex(value)` \u2014 full 64-char lower-case digest.\n\nCentralizing it guarantees the DTO's exposed `identityKey` is exactly the value the server compares against.\n\n**`mapper/OwnerMapper.identityKey`** \u2014 now delegates to `IdentityKeys.identityKey(...)`, so the DTO field is the 64-hex key instead of the old plaintext `telephone|email|householdId` string.\n\n**`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1`:**\n- `deriveIdentityKey(telephone, email, lastName)` now delegates to the util (was plaintext concatenation with `householdId`).\n- `rejectDuplicateIdentity` derives each existing owner's key from its `lastName` (not `householdId`); still filters to non-deleted owners, and the email-domain blocklist still runs first (in `normalizeEmail`, before this check).\n- `findPossibleDuplicateOf` now soft-matches when the `identityKey` **differs** but `soundex(lastName)` **and** postcode both match \u2014 so two owners with the same surname/postcode but different telephones become a soft match rather than a 409.\n- `addOwner` computes the identity key once and threads it into both the reject check and the soft-match check.\n\nBehavioural effects, all per spec: the separate household-duplicate 409 (already consolidated into the identity key) stays gone; telephone differences no longer make a hard household duplicate; and the soft match now keys on the phonetic surname code plus postcode.",
